  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With the recent happenings as of late, one particular thing I've complained about quite a while is the Example Central. It definitely feels that there's a push for learning U# while Udon Graph is becoming an after-thought. I, along with others, don't have time to learn U#. It took even learning Udon a long time for me personally since I had no experience with it and only made game worlds back then because SDK2's Triggers made it so easily understandable. That being said--\n\nPlease for current and future SDK3 world examples-- include graphs. I'm a stupid person. I rely heavily on visual. I'm sure others share the same sentiment. But when I tried to learn about how to use Persistence when it released and it was in U#? It highly discouraged me from even trying game worlds for a bit again. Others share the same sentiment.\n\nTl;dr\n\nCurrent and future SDK3 examples in Example Central, please add Udon Graph example versions, thank you very much.",
